{"id":"27786514a7d442bd","group":"58","path":"58/batch08/58-df-two-cardinal.md","title":"Two-Cardinal Transfer","display":"df-two-cardinal — Two-Cardinal Transfer","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-two-cardinal","aliases":["58-df-two-cardinal","Two-Cardinal Transfer"],"display":"df-two-cardinal — Two-Cardinal Transfer","depends_on":["[[../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]","[[../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-two-cardinal"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-two-cardinal</span><span>Two-Cardinal Transfer</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-two-cardinal — Two-Cardinal Transfer"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md\">../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula.md\">../batch17/58-df-formula.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"8b6a90316aad78a4\" href=\"?note=8b6a90316aad78a4\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md\">../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T,\\Sigma,U,\\kappa,\\lambda,\\kappa&#39;,\\lambda&#39;\\in V\">\\(T,\\Sigma,U,\\kappa,\\lambda,\\kappa&#39;,\\lambda&#39;\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\">\\(T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\)</span> (theory, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula.md\">../batch17/58-df-formula.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U\\in\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{rel}}\\land a_{\\mathrm{rel}}(U)=1\">\\(U\\in\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{rel}}\\land a_{\\mathrm{rel}}(U)=1\\)</span> (distinguished unary predicate symbol)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\\subseteq V\">\\(\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S\\subseteq V\\)</span> (cardinal predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md\">../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Model}\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{Model}\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> (model predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"8b6a90316aad78a4\" href=\"?note=8b6a90316aad78a4\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md\">../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Univ}:V\\to V\">\\(\\mathrm{Univ}:V\\to V\\)</span> (underlying-universe operator on structures)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{TwoCardinalTransfer}_S\\subseteq V^7\">\\(\\operatorname{TwoCardinalTransfer}_S\\subseteq V^7\\)</span> (transfer predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}two\\text{-}cardinal} \\vdash \\operatorname{TwoCardinalTransfer}_S(T,\\Sigma,U,\\kappa,\\lambda,\\kappa&#39;,\\lambda&#39;) \\leftrightarrow T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\land U\\in\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{rel}}\\land a_{\\mathrm{rel}}(U)=1\\land\\bigwedge_{\\mu\\in\\{\\kappa,\\lambda,\\kappa&#39;,\\lambda&#39;\\}}\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\mu)\\land\\lambda\\leq\\kappa\\land\\lambda&#39;\\leq\\kappa&#39;\\land\\forall\\mathcal M\\;\\left(\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathcal M,T)\\land|\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal M)|=\\kappa\\land|U^{\\mathcal M}|=\\lambda\\to\\exists\\mathcal N\\;(\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathcal N,T)\\land|\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal N)|=\\kappa&#39;\\land|U^{\\mathcal N}|=\\lambda&#39;)\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}two\\text{-}cardinal} \\vdash \\operatorname{TwoCardinalTransfer}_S(T,\\Sigma,U,\\kappa,\\lambda,\\kappa&#39;,\\lambda&#39;) \\leftrightarrow T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\land U\\in\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{rel}}\\land a_{\\mathrm{rel}}(U)=1\\land\\bigwedge_{\\mu\\in\\{\\kappa,\\lambda,\\kappa&#39;,\\lambda&#39;\\}}\\mathrm{Cardinal}_S(\\mu)\\land\\lambda\\leq\\kappa\\land\\lambda&#39;\\leq\\kappa&#39;\\land\\forall\\mathcal M\\;\\left(\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathcal M,T)\\land|\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal M)|=\\kappa\\land|U^{\\mathcal M}|=\\lambda\\to\\exists\\mathcal N\\;(\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathcal N,T)\\land|\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal N)|=\\kappa&#39;\\land|U^{\\mathcal N}|=\\lambda&#39;)\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The pair records both the size of the whole universe and the size of the distinguished unary predicate; ordinary downward Löwenheim–Skolem is therefore not the definition.</li>\n<li>Forcing consistency and Morley categoricity clauses are related theorems, not part of this transfer predicate definition.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Keisler, Logic with the Quantifier &quot;There exist uncountably many&quot;</li>\n<li>Shelah, Classification Theory</li>\n<li>Chang and Keisler, Model Theory</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch11/58-df-cardinal.md","status":"resolved","id":"5fb1c2241d1943d1","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":